        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "The pyknotid package has been successfully compiled and installed from source with full Numpy 2.3.0 compatibility. Here's a summary of the changes made:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. **Cython Extensions Compiled Successfully**\nAll four Cython extensions now build and work:\n- `pyknotid.spacecurves.chelpers`\n- `pyknotid.spacecurves.ccomplexity`\n- `pyknotid.simplify.coctree`\n- `pyknotid.cinvariants`\n\n### 2. **Numpy 2.0+ Compatibility Fixes**\n\n| File | Fix |\n|------|-----|\n| `pyknotid/make/torus.py` | `from fractions import gcd` → `from math import gcd` |\n| `pyknotid/make/periodic_knot.py` | `dtype=n.float` → `dtype=n.float64` |\n| `pyknotid/spacecurves/spacecurve.py` | `dtype=n.float` → `dtype=n.float64`, `.astype(n.float)` → `.astype(n.float64)` |\n| `pyknotid/invariants.py` | `n.complex` → `n.complex128`, `n.float` → `n.float64` |\n| `pyknotid/representations/representation.py` | Added `import numpy as np`, replaced deprecated `n.int`, `n.round`, `n.abs`, `n.max`, `n.min`, `n.array`, `n.vstack`, `n.cross`, `n.linalg.norm`, `n.arange` with `np.` equivalents |\n| `pyknotid/make/torus.py` | Fixed `np.linspace` call with float `divisions` → `int(divisions)` |\n| `pyknotid/representations/representation.py` | Fixed planarity graph attribute access: `data['pos']` → `data.get('pos', data.get('vertex_position', data.get('edge_position')))` (and similar for 'start'/'end') |\n\n### 3. **Test Results**\nAll 18 tests pass (excluding the two ignored test files as requested):\n- `tests/test_knot.py` - 2 ",
